msgid "EU GARAN label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:380
msgid "The label of the commercial guarantee of durability that a producer can offer: free of charge, for the whole product and for more than two years. It is the producer's, so it goes per product: fill in the EU GARAN tab of the product with what the producer gives you, and the plugin draws the official label with it. It is shown on the product page, before the place-order button, as a line in the cart and in the order email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:383
msgid "On the product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:387
msgid "The full label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:388
msgid "The nested label, which opens the full one on the first click"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:397
msgid "Before the place-order button it is always the nested label, one per product, as the guidelines allow where space is short; in the email it is always the full one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:402
#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:165
msgid "PDF invoices"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:405
msgid "Invoice"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:409
msgid "Add a reminder of the legal guarantee, and the EU GARAN label of each line, to the invoices"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:412
msgid "For the invoices of PDF Invoices & Packing Slips for WooCommerce, by WP Overnight. The notice itself already travels as a PDF with the order email; the invoice gets a short reminder with the Your Europe link and the national note."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:414
msgid "That plugin is not active on this site, so this setting does nothing for now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:423
#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:455
#: includes/clases/bloques.php:37
#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:177
msgid "Wording"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:427
#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:175
msgid "Wording that opens it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:432
msgid "Used by every placement. The notice opens on the first click on it, which is the pattern the Commission illustrates. Leave it empty for the default wording."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:435
msgid "The Commission's guidelines describe this as \"a sentence informing consumers about their legal guarantee rights\", and every example they give is written text. They do provide a compact graphic for the GARAN label, and deliberately none for this notice. Icon only keeps the wording for screen readers and in the tooltip, but a visitor on a phone never sees it, since there is no hover on a touch screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:441
msgid "National note"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:442
msgid "The official notice says \"minimum two years\" because that is the European floor, and the file may not be edited. Where your country grants longer, tell the customer beside the notice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:445
#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:176
msgid "Show the note"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:449
msgid "Show a national note next to the notice"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:459
msgid "Leave it empty for the default, which depends on the country of your shop: the three years of Article 120.1 TRLGDCU in Spain, the three years of Decree-Law 84/2021 in Portugal, or the three years to claim of the Swedish Consumer Sales Act."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:464
#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:178
msgid "Terms and conditions page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:487
#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:494
msgid "— None —"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:499
msgid "Linked from the national note, and the page the menu item points at. Defaults to the Terms and conditions page of WooCommerce, which is not the same thing as the privacy policy page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:505
#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:184
msgid "Your guarantee terms"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:506
msgid "The official notice is the European summary and cannot be edited. What it does not say is what your shop does: how long the guarantee runs here, how a customer claims it and who they write to. That text is yours, and the plugin only gives you a starting point for it."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the shortcode, already wrapped in a code tag.
#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:518
#, php-format
msgid "Shown by the %s shortcode. Leave it empty to use the suggested text, which appears greyed out above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:524
msgid "Read it before you publish it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:525
msgid "It describes what the law already grants, but only you know how your shop handles a claim, and the text has no legal value until you have made it yours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:531
msgid "Shortcodes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/ajustes.php:535
msgid "The official notice printed in the page, at full size. For a page devoted to the guarantee, where the notice is the content rather than a reminder."
