msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:103
msgid "not the site. A shop read in German serves the German notice. Catalan, Basque and Galician fall back on the Spanish notice rather than the English one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:104
msgid "opens the very notice a visitor would see right now, in the language named beside it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:105
msgid "It opens on the first click"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:105
msgid "in a modal, the pattern the Commission's guidelines illustrate, built with the browser's own popover API and no JavaScript at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:110
#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:160
msgid "Where it is shown"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:112
msgid "The obligation is to display the notice at shop level, so one placement reaching every page is enough. Switch them all off and the plugin warns you on the dashboard, because then the notice is not reaching anybody."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:113
msgid "floats over every page of the shop, in any of six positions. On out of the box, at the bottom right, and on its own it satisfies the obligation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:114
msgid "added as the last item of the menu you choose. With a page chosen below it is an ordinary link, which is what a theme knows how to style; with no page it opens the modal instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:115
msgid "adds it to the footer of every page, wherever your theme prints the footer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:122
msgid "Every placement carries its own appearance, so the floating button can shout and the menu item can be indistinguishable from the rest of the menu. Out of the box nothing is imposed at all, which is what keeps the notice readable on a dark theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:123
msgid "text, icon and text, or icon only. The Commission describes the notice as a sentence, and every example in its guidelines is written text, so text only is the recommended answer. Icon only keeps the wording for screen readers and in the tooltip, but a visitor on a phone never sees it, since there is no hover on a touch screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:124
msgid "whatever surrounds it, a link of this theme, a button of this theme, or colours you choose."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:125
msgid "nothing of the plugin's goes on the element, which inherits everything from the theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:126
msgid "hands the element the theme's own button classes, so the theme paints it, hover and focus included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:127
msgid "reads the link colours out of the theme, which a block theme answers through its theme.json and a classic theme not at all. With no answer the element simply inherits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:128
msgid "opens the text, background and hover colours, and the font size in pixels. Each colour has an Inherit box next to it, and ticked it is the theme that decides; an empty font size leaves the size to the theme as well."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:135
msgid "Both of these are WooCommerce's: without it there is no checkout to print above and no order email to go into, so the two settings are hidden rather than shown doing nothing. What you had configured is kept and comes back the day WooCommerce does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:136
msgid "shows it above the place-order button of the classic checkout, and under the form when the shop uses the Checkout block, where it is outside the React root and survives. The Commission's guidelines ask for the checkout page, prominently, not a precise spot."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:137
msgid "a sentence that opens the notice on the first click, as the Commission's guidelines illustrate, or the whole notice with nothing to click. Part of the German doctrine reads the law as asking for the second at the checkout; if you sell in Germany or Austria, or prefer to be on the safe side, choose it. The image links to itself, so it can be opened at full size from a narrow column."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:138
msgid "includes the notice in the emails the customer receives, as an image, since an email client cannot open a modal, and attaches the Commission's official PDF in the customer's language. Your own copies of the emails are left alone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:139
msgid "leaves the notice out of purchases made only of virtual products, since its legal guarantee covers goods. Applies to the checkout, the cart, the product page, the order email and the invoice. The floating button, the menu and the footer remind the whole shop and stay where they are."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:140
msgid "leaves a private note on each order saying how and in which language the notice was shown at the checkout, which EU GARAN labels were shown, and the first email that carried the official PDF. It is your proof if a customer or an authority ever asks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:147
msgid "Neither is required, since the obligation is met at shop level. They put the notice next to the decision to buy, which is one of the places the Commission's guidelines illustrate. Both are off out of the box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:148
msgid "under the add-to-cart button, as the sentence that opens the notice or as the whole notice. It works with classic themes and with block themes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:149
msgid "under the cart totals, in the classic cart and after the Cart block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:156
msgid "The label of the commercial guarantee of durability a producer can offer: free of charge, for the whole product and for more than two years. The guarantee is the producer's, so the label goes per product, with what the producer gives you; the shop should not go looking for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:157
msgid "EU GARAN tab"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:157
msgid "in the product data box: the duration in years (more than two, in whole or half years such as 3, 5 or 2,5), the producer and the model identifier, the three editable fields of the label. The label stays off until the three are there. Each variation can set its own and inherits the rest from the product."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:158
msgid "if the producer gave you the label already filled in, upload it in the same tab and it is shown as it came instead of being drawn."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:159
msgid "How it is drawn"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:159
msgid "on the Commission's own template, with only the three fields filled in and in the typeface the guidelines name, Inter. A value too long for its box is printed smaller rather than over the QR code, and the product screen warns you when that happens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:160
msgid "on the product page, as the full label or as the nested one that opens it; before the place-order button, nested, one per product; as a line of text in the cart; on the order screen; and in the order email as an image, which needs the GD extension of PHP. Site Health tells you if it is missing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:167
msgid "For the invoices of PDF Invoices & Packing Slips for WooCommerce, by WP Overnight. The notice itself already travels as a PDF with the order email; the invoice gets a short reminder of the legal guarantee with the Your Europe link and the national note, and the EU GARAN label of each line in words."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:172
msgid "Wording and the national note"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:174
msgid "The notice is the Commission's and cannot be touched. These two texts are yours: the line that opens it and the national note printed beside it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:175
msgid "used by every placement, and the title of the modal. Leave it empty for the default wording."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:176
msgid "the official notice says \"minimum two years\" because that is the European floor and the file may not be edited. Where your own country grants longer, this is how you tell the customer, next to the notice and never inside it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:177
msgid "the text of that note. Empty, it states the three years of Article 120.1 TRLGDCU in Spain, the three years of Decree-Law 84/2021 in Portugal or the three years to claim of the Swedish Consumer Sales Act, and it arrives switched on when the shop sells from one of those three countries. The country is read from your WooCommerce base location, never guessed from the language."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:178
msgid "linked from the national note, and the page the menu item points at. Defaults to the Terms and conditions page of WooCommerce, which is not the same thing as the privacy policy page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:179
msgid "creates a published page holding the official notice and your guarantee terms, and selects it here. Uninstalling the plugin never deletes it: it is your content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:186
msgid "The official notice is the European summary. What it does not say is what your shop does: how long the guarantee runs here, how a customer claims it and who they write to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:187
msgid "your own terms, shown by the [apg_guarantee_terms] shortcode. Leave it empty to use the suggested text, which appears greyed out in the field. Read it before you publish it: it describes what the law already grants, but only you know how your shop handles a claim, and it has no legal value until you have made it yours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:192
msgid "Shortcodes and blocks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:194
msgid "For placing the notice somewhere the settings above do not reach. The block editor has the same three as blocks (Legal guarantee notice, Legal guarantee button and Guarantee terms), plus the EU GARAN label block for the product template."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:195
msgid "the official notice printed in the page, at full size, with the Your Europe link and the national note under it. For a page devoted to the guarantee, where the notice is the content rather than a reminder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:196
msgid "your guarantee terms, the text above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-guarantee-help.php:197
msgid "the button that opens the notice in a modal. Accepts label, class and style, the same three styles as the placements."
msgstr ""

